# Exact downstream requests in order (file ops between steps)

### step 1: external host file op — file-write fake kimi auth json (external)
(run3/run/auths/oracle-fake-kimi.json created/deleted; sleep 2s for the watcher)

### step 2: 30 auth-files list with file present
GET /v0/management/auth-files HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1




### step 3: external host file op — file-delete (external)
(run3/run/auths/oracle-fake-kimi.json created/deleted; sleep 2s for the watcher)

### step 4: 30 auth-files list after delete
GET /v0/management/auth-files HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1



